# Architecture Rules

Use a pnpm/Turborepo monorepo.

- `apps/web`: Next.js 16 App Router, TypeScript strict mode.
- `services/ai`: FastAPI API and Celery worker.
- `packages/db`: Drizzle schema, migrations, and typed queries.
- `packages/domain`: domain services independent of UI.
- `packages/contracts`: Zod schemas and generated OpenAPI types.
- `packages/ui`: accessible shared UI.

Use PostgreSQL 18 with pgvector, Redis, and S3-compatible object storage.

The web app is a modular monolith. Do not create separate microservices for Motif Explorer, Hue Seer, Lasem Guru, or Dress Weaver in Year 1.

The browser must not call the AI service directly. Next.js is the authenticated backend-for-frontend.

Every protected operation validates authorization inside its server action, route handler, and/or domain service. Proxy checks are not sufficient authorization.

Long-running image, embedding, export, and rendering work must be asynchronous and idempotent.
